 LIGHTING",0,0,0,0],[11406889,"2021-04-07","EXTERIOR LIGHTING",0,0,0,0],[11394480,"2021-02-03","SERVICE BRAKES",0,0,0,0],[11394325,"2021-02-02","FUEL/PROPULSION SYSTEM",0,0,0,0],[11377272,"2020-12-01","POWER TRAIN",0,0,0,0],[11374100,"2020-11-11","EXTERIOR LIGHTING",0,0,0,0],[11343643,"2020-08-06","UNKNOWN OR OTHER",0,0,0,0],[11340406,"2020-07-20","POWER TRAIN",0,0,0,0]],"recalls":[{"campaign":"20E068000","received":"2020-09-17","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"EQUIPMENT","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling all Honda Genuine Accessory Tonneau Covers, part number 08Z07-T6Z-100F, sold for installation on 2017-2020 Ridgeline trucks.  If the tonneau cover is not properly secured in the open or closed position, wind resistance may cause the cover to flip and buckle.  If this occurs, the hinges between the center and rear panel may deform, possibly allowing the rear panel to separate from the vehicle.","consequence":"A separated panel may become a road hazard, increasing the risk of crash or injury.","remedy":"Honda will notify all registered owners of 2017-2020 Honda Ridgelines, and dealers will install tethers onto any Honda Genuine Accessory Tonneau Cover to prevent panel separation and apply warning labels, free of charge.  In addition, an updated accessory user's information manual will be provided.  The recall began October 26, 2020.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is F8M.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":151343,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=20E068000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":5,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"9999","make":"HONDA","model":"HARD TONNEAU COVERS"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"21V932000","received":"2021-11-29","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"STRUCTURE:BODY:HOOD","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2019 Passport, 2016-2019 Pilot, and 2017-2020 Ridgeline vehicles.  The hood latch striker may become damaged and separate from the hood, which can result in the hood opening while driving.","consequence":"A hood that opens while driving can obstruct the driver's view and increase the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will either repair the hood latch striker, or replace the hood if necessary, free of charge.  Owner notification letters were mailed January 18, 2022.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is PBV.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":724826,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=21V932000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":9,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2016","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V174000","received":"2023-03-16","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"VISIBILITY:REARVIEW MIRRORS/DEVICES:EXTERIOR","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co) is recalling certain 2020-2021 Pilot and Ridgeline, and 2020-2022 Passport and Odyssey vehicles.  The heating pads behind both side-view mirrors may not be bonded properly, allowing the mirror glass to detach.  As such, these vehicles fail to comply with the requirements of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard number 111, \"Rear Visibility.\"","consequence":"Detached mirror glass can reduce driver visibility, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace both left and right side-view mirrors, free of charge.  Owner letters were mailed January 17, 2024.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is FE5.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":339404,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V174000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":10,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V458000","received":"2023-06-29","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"SERVICE BRAKES, HYDRAULIC:FOUNDATION COMPONENTS:MASTER CYLINDER","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2020-2021 Civic, 2020-2023 Ridgeline, 2021-2023 Passport, 2021-2022 Pilot, and 2020 Acura MDX vehicles.  The tie rod fastener that connects the brake booster and the brake master cylinder may have been improperly assembled during manufacturing, which can cause the brake master cylinder to separate from the booster assembly.","consequence":"Brake master cylinder separation can cause a loss of brake function and increase the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will inspect and repair the brake booster assembly as necessary, free of charge.  Owner notification letters were mailed August 7, 2023.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for this recall are VEU, AEV, and ZET.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":124077,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V458000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":12,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2023","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2023","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V858000","received":"2023-12-19","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE:DELIVERY:FUEL PUMP","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2013-2023 Honda Accord, Civic Coupe, Civic Sedan, Civic Hatchback, Civic Type R, CR-V, HR-V, Ridgeline, Odyssey, Acura ILX, MDX, MDX Hybrid, RDX, RLX, TLX, 2019-2022 Honda Insight, Passport, 2020 Honda CR-V Hybrid, 2018-2019 Honda Clarity PHEV, Fit, and 2015-2020 Honda Accord Hybrid, Pilot, Acura NSX vehicles.  The fuel pump inside the fuel tank may fail.","consequence":"Fuel pump failure can cause an engine stall while driving, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the fuel pump module, free of charge.  Owner letters were mailed September 6, 2024.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for this recall are KGC and KGD.  This recall is an expansion of NHTSA recall numbers 21V-215 and 20V-314.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":2490460,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V858000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":107,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"ILX"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"NSX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"FIT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"ILX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"NSX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"24V064000","received":"2024-02-01","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"AIR BAGS:SENSOR:OCCUPANT CLASSIFICATION:FRONT PASSENGER","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2020-2022 Pilot, Accord, Civic sedan, HR-V, Odyssey, 2020 Civic coupe, Fit, 2021-2022 Civic hatchback, 2021 Civic Type R, Insight, 2020-2021 CR-V, CR-V Hybrid, Passport, Ridgeline, Accord Hybrid, 2020 Acura MDX, 2022 Acura MDX, 2020-2022 Acura RDX, and 2020-2021 Acura TLX vehicles.  The front passenger seat weight sensor may crack and short circuit, failing to suppress the air bag as intended.","consequence":"An air bag that deploys unintentionally during a crash can increase the risk of injury.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the seat weight sensors, free of charge.  Owner notification letters were mailed March 28, 2024.  This is a phased recall.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for these recalls are XHP and VHQ.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":750114,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=24V064000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":35,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2022","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"},{"year":"2022","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"},{"year":"2021","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2021","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V HYBRID"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"24V321000","received":"2024-05-10","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"BACK OVER PREVENTION: SENSING SYSTEM: CAMERA","summary":"Honda (America Honda Motor Co) is recalling certain 2020-2024 Ridgeline vehicles.  The rearview camera (RVC) tailgate wire harness may fatigue and break, which can prevent the rearview camera image from displaying.","consequence":"A rearview camera that does not display an image can reduce the driver's rear view, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the RVC tailgate wire harness, free of charge.  Owner letters were mailed November 8, 2024.  Owners may contact Honda service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is YI7.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":187290,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=24V321000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":6,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2024","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2023","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2025","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"26V332000","received":"2026-05-22","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"AIR BAGS:SENSOR:OCCUPANT CLASSIFICATION:FRONT PASSENGER","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2018-2021, 2023 Acura TLX, 2019-2024 RDX, 2017-2020, 2022-2026 MDX, 2017-2021, 2023, 2025 Honda Ridgeline, 2017-2022 Pilot, 2019-2021 Passport, 2018-2026 Odyssey, 2019-2022 Insight, 2019-2021 HR-V, 2018-2020 Fit, 2020-2022 CR-V Hybrid, 2017-2022 CR-V, 2017-2018, 2021 Civic Type R, 2017-2021 Civic hatchback, 2016-2020 Civic coupe, 2016-2022 Civic, 2017-2022 Accord Hybrid, and 2016-2022 Accord vehicles. The front passenger seat weight sensor may crack and short circuit, which can cause the air bags to deploy unintentionally during a crash.","consequence":"Air bags that deploy unintentionally during a crash increase the risk of injury.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the seat weight sensors, free of charge. Owner notification letters were mailed July 7, 2026. Owners may contact Honda's customer service at 1-888-234-2138. Honda's numbers for this recall are BOL, WO9, OOA, WOM, XOH, NOC, POD, BOE, UOF, POB, EOG, AOI, QO8, TOJ, DO7, and SOK. This recall expands previous NHTSA recall number 24V064. Vehicle Identification Numbers (VINs) involved in this recall will be searchable on NHTSA.gov beginning May 29, 2026.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":98892,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=26V332000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":92,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2021","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2021","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model"